course: dictionary
lesson: 363
title: Antibodies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An antibody is a special protein that your body's immune system makes. It sticks to germs, such as viruses and bacteria, and helps destroy them. «White blood cells fight germs and make antibodies.» So white blood cells are the makers, and antibodies are the tools they make.
explain: «Each kind of antibody matches a certain germ, like a key fits a lock.» The clues are "matches" and "fits", so one antibody works against one kind of germ, not every germ. Check by swapping in your meaning: "each special protein fits one kind of germ exactly" still makes sense.
explain: Vaccines use this same idea. «A vaccine teaches the body this lesson safely» by showing it a weakened, killed or harmless part of a germ. The body then makes antibodies without you getting really ill, so it is ready if the real germ ever arrives.
fact: An antibody is a special protein made by the immune system.
fact: Antibodies stick to germs, like viruses and bacteria, and help destroy them.
fact: White blood cells fight germs and make antibodies.
fact: Each kind of antibody matches one kind of germ, like a key fits a lock.
fact: «Make antibodies» means to produce them, and «antibodies against» a germ means antibodies that fight that particular germ.
fact: Vaccines teach your body to make antibodies before you meet the real germ, so you do not get as ill.
exercise: «White blood cells fight germs and make antibodies.» What is an antibody? | A bone in your arm | *A special protein that sticks to germs and helps destroy them | A white blood cell | A type of germ
exercise: «Each kind of antibody matches a certain germ, like a key fits a lock.» What does matches mean here? | Makes the germ bigger | Runs away from germs | Is the same thing as a germ | *Fits one particular germ exactly
exercise: «A vaccine teaches the body this lesson safely.» What is a vaccine's job? | Gives you the real germ so you become really ill | *Teaches the body to make antibodies before the real germ arrives | Cleans germs out of your blood | Makes you grow taller
test: Which of these is an antibody? | A germ that makes you ill | A white blood cell | *A special protein that sticks to germs | A snake's fang
test: Why does a vaccine help you not get ill? | It gives you snake venom | It makes germs stronger | It stops white blood cells from existing | *Your body makes antibodies before it meets the real germ
exam: «Antivenom is made by giving horses small doses of venom and collecting the antibodies their bodies make.» What is antivenom made from? | Germs grown in a laboratory | *Antibodies collected from animals such as horses | Bones from horses | Pure water
